# rpg/art/doll/clips/actions/bow.clip: PROPOSED by SLICE-ARMS (2026-10-23); SLICE-DOLL owns and commits it. The bow
# (STYLE_P2 25.8 item 6): the drawn idle, the draw (nock, chest, cheek over the windup, the cheek held as the loaded pose)
# and the release (80 ms: the Twang and the string's blur), four facings. Facing up the bow is behind the body. The drawn
# walk and run (variants 1 and 2) are the sword's drawn lines with armL=bw_low armR=bw_low held=low.
# (P2c slice iteration 1, INTEGRATE) SLICE-ARMS's proposed lines committed: the drawn idle / walk / run moved to `part drawn`,
# every clip gated `when bow` (a fighter's: a civil trade with the same tool keeps the generic clips).
# (P2c wave 2, ACTIONS-2H) `when bow,!bow-crossbow`: the crossbow's lines are crossbow.clip's.
# (wave-2 fix round, ACTIONS r1, PLAN D81: no weapon pixel more than 2 rows below the sole row) the longbow is a row too long
# for the low hold facing D / U on the breath and step frames (its lower limb 3 rows under the soles): it holds the drawn
# idle and walk facing D / U at the nock (bw_nock, held=nock), the bow a row higher with the arrow on the string.

body man
